  "chapter": {
    "number": 91,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(92) A Psalm of a Song for the Sabbath-day."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "It is a good thing to give thanks to the Lord, and to sing praises to your name, O you Most High;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to proclaim your mercy in the morning, and your truth by night,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "on a lute of ten strings, with a song on the harp.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you, O Lord, have made me glad with your work: and in the operations of your hands will I exult.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How have your works been magnified, O Lord! your thoughts are very deep.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A foolish man will not know, and a senseless man will not understand this.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When the sinners spring up as the grass, and all the workers of iniquity",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 176
          },
          {
            "text": "have watched; it is that they may be utterly destroyed for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, O Lord, are most high for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 177
          },
          {
            "text": "For, behold, your enemies shall perish; and all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But my horn shall be exalted as the horn of a unicorn; and my old age with rich",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 178
          },
          {
            "text": "mercy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And my eye has seen my enemies, and my ear shall hear the wicked that rise up against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The righteous shall flourish as a palm tree: he shall be increased as the cedar in Libanus.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They that are planted in the house of the Lord shall flourish in the courts of our God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Then shall they be increased in a",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 179
          },
          {
            "text": "fine old age; and they shall be prosperous; that they may declare",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "that the Lord my God is righteous, and there is no iniquity in him.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 176,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Perhaps, 'come to light'.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 91,
          "verse": 7
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 177,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. + for behold your enemies, O Lord, as in Heb.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 91,
          "verse": 9
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 178,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. oil. See Ps. 88:20.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 91,
          "verse": 10
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 179,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. fat.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 91,
          "verse": 14
        }
      }
    ]
